      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "🚨 Securing Our Border: The \"Puebla Tree\" Gap is CLOSED! 🚨\n\nFor years, the Otay Mountain Wilderness in San Diego, California, was plagued by dangerous cartel enforcers and bandits operating near the \"Puebla Tree\" border gap. As recently as 2024, these criminal organizations patrolled near the international border, ensuring cartel \"plaza\" payments were made before crossing. They exploited these easily traversable gaps to cross into the U.S., where they would rob, kidnap, and extort anyone they encountered.\n\nToday, that has changed. Thanks to the relentless efforts of our @USBPChiefSDC agents, our partnerships, and the strategic infrastructure improvements, the \"Puebla Tree\" border gap is now CLOSED. We've sent a clear message: these criminal activities are no longer tolerated, and cartels are not welcome here. Our commitment to securing our communities and protecting those along the border remains unwavering.",
      "text_resolved": "🚨 Securing Our Border: The \"Puebla Tree\" Gap is CLOSED! 🚨\n\nFor years, the Otay Mountain Wilderness in San Diego, California, was plagued by dangerous cartel enforcers and bandits operating near the \"Puebla Tree\" border gap. As recently as 2024, these criminal organizations patrolled near the international border, ensuring cartel \"plaza\" payments were made before crossing. They exploited these easily traversable gaps to cross into the U.S., where they would rob, kidnap, and extort anyone they encountered.\n\nToday, that has changed. Thanks to the relentless efforts of our @USBPChiefSDC agents, our partnerships, and the strategic infrastructure improvements, the \"Puebla Tree\" border gap is now CLOSED. We've sent a clear message: these criminal activities are no longer tolerated, and cartels are not welcome here. Our commitment to securing our communities and protecting those along the border remains unwavering.",
